---@class ManageAccessibilityUpdates : ReflectReference
---  Determines whether Bevy's ECS updates the accessibility tree.
--- 
---  This [`Resource`] tells Bevy internals whether it should be handling
---  `AccessKit` updates (`true`), or if something else is doing that (`false`).
--- 
---  It defaults to `true`. So, by default, Bevy is configured to maintain the
---  `AccessKit` tree.
--- 
---  Set to `false` in cases where an external GUI library is sending
---  accessibility updates instead. When this option is set inconsistently with
---  that requirement, the external library and ECS will generate conflicting
---  updates.
--- 
---  [`Resource`]: bevy_ecs::resource::Resource
---@field  [1] boolean
ManageAccessibilityUpdates = {}

---@param payload ManageAccessibilityUpdates.Fields
--- The fields of the type, keyed by name or index, or a list of the fields in order.
---@return ManageAccessibilityUpdates
function ManageAccessibilityUpdates.new(payload) end



---@class AppExit : ReflectReference
---  A [`Message`] that indicates the [`App`] should exit. If one or more of these are present at the end of an update,
---  the [runner](App::set_runner) will end and ([maybe](App::run)) return control to the caller.
--- 
---  This message can be used to detect when an exit is requested. Make sure that systems listening
---  for this message run before the current update ends.
--- 
---  # Portability
---  This type is roughly meant to map to a standard definition of a process exit code (0 means success, not 0 means error). Due to portability concerns
---  (see [`ExitCode`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/process/struct.ExitCode.html) and [`process::exit`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/process/fn.exit.html#))
---  we only allow error codes between 1 and [255](u8::MAX).
---@field  Success AppExit.UnitVariant
---@field  Error AppExit.Error
AppExit = {}

---@param payload AppExit.Fields
--- The fields of the type, keyed by name or index, or a list of the fields in order.
---@return AppExit
